WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.536
So I'm thinking about hardware devices

00:00:02.656 --> 00:00:04.876
as essentially physical representatives

00:00:04.876 --> 00:00:06.079
of these cloud services.

00:00:06.079 --> 00:00:09.345
Which makes them very different than traditional

00:00:09.345 --> 00:00:10.671
consumer electronics.

00:00:10.671 --> 00:00:14.206
So historically a company made an electronic product.

00:00:14.206 --> 00:00:18.015
Say a turntable. Then they found
people who would sell it for them.

00:00:18.015 --> 00:00:20.526
Then they advertised it heavily. And people bought them.

00:00:20.526 --> 00:00:21.736
And that was the end of their relationship

00:00:21.736 --> 00:00:25.036
with that customer until they were able to convince

00:00:25.036 --> 00:00:27.372
that person to buy another one.

00:00:27.372 --> 00:00:31.516
So the entire value of that relationship

00:00:31.516 --> 00:00:34.074
had to be packaged within the device itself.

00:00:34.074 --> 00:00:35.295
My pet theory is that

00:00:35.296 --> 00:00:37.676
that's why they used to put heavy metal plates

00:00:37.676 --> 00:00:39.496
into consumer electronics. So they would feel like

00:00:39.496 --> 00:00:41.708
they were getting more value out of them.

00:00:41.716 --> 00:00:45.276
With the Internet of Things, the sale of the device

00:00:45.276 --> 00:00:47.295
is actually just the beginning of the relationship.

00:00:47.296 --> 00:00:50.316
It's not the end of the relationship,
it's the beginning of the relationship.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:54.376
And the physical thing actually holds almost no value

00:00:54.376 --> 00:00:58.036
for either the consumer or the manufacturer.

00:00:58.036 --> 00:01:02.276
Value now shifts to services. And the devices:

00:01:02.276 --> 00:01:04.456
the device is the software applications.

00:01:04.471 --> 00:01:06.166
You know, the website, the apps

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:07.845
that are used to access them.

00:01:07.845 --> 00:01:09.392
I call those things avatars.

00:01:09.396 --> 00:01:11.576
They're physical representatives of a thing that's

00:01:11.576 --> 00:01:15.196
up in the clouds right? I also want to steal it back

00:01:15.196 --> 00:01:19.676
from the VR people. That was totally wrong.

00:01:19.676 --> 00:01:23.576
So anyway, a camera becomes a really good appliance

00:01:23.576 --> 00:01:26.746
for taking photos for Instagram.

00:01:26.746 --> 00:01:28.129
My TV becomes a really nice way

00:01:28.136 --> 00:01:30.596
to display Instagram photos that you don't have to log

00:01:30.596 --> 00:01:32.976
into every time; and you can show people at a party.

00:01:32.976 --> 00:01:34.996
A phone becomes a really convenient way

00:01:35.056 --> 00:01:38.436
both to take photos and to check your friends' photos,

00:01:38.445 --> 00:01:42.046
photo streams (or Kanye's) when you're on the road.

00:01:42.046 --> 00:01:45.216
Hardware, the physical things, in this situation

00:01:45.216 --> 00:01:47.236
becomes simultaneously more specialized

00:01:47.236 --> 00:01:49.536
and de-valued as people

00:01:49.536 --> 00:01:52.056
see through each device to the service it represents.

00:01:52.056 --> 00:01:53.356
People don't care about the device.

00:01:53.516 --> 00:01:54.736
They care about the service.

00:01:54.736 --> 00:01:57.756
The avatars exist in order to get better

00:01:57.756 --> 00:02:00.036
value out of the service.

00:02:00.036 --> 00:02:03.896
Amazon really gets this. So here's a telling older ad

00:02:03.896 --> 00:02:06.976
from Amazon for the Kindle. What it's saying is:

00:02:06.976 --> 00:02:10.436
look, use whatever device you want. We don't care.

00:02:10.436 --> 00:02:12.276
As long as you stay loyal to our service.

00:02:12.276 --> 00:02:14.236
You can buy one of our specialized devices

00:02:14.236 --> 00:02:17.596
that we lose money on every time (on purpose)

00:02:17.596 --> 00:02:20.416
because the value is in the service.

00:02:20.416 --> 00:02:22.436
But you can use some other way to access our services,

00:02:22.436 --> 00:02:24.936
and we don't have to lose money on the device.

00:02:24.936 --> 00:02:28.476
When Fire was launched, it was originally "Kindle Fire".

00:02:28.476 --> 00:02:30.796
Now you know you have Fire Stick and Fire Phone

00:02:30.796 --> 00:02:32.776
RIP (not really in IP) but anyway...

00:02:32.776 --> 00:02:38.776
those of you--only like two of us would get that joke--

00:02:38.776 --> 00:02:43.276
when Fire was released Bezos even called it a service.

00:02:43.276 --> 00:02:44.266
It is not a device.

00:02:44.266 --> 00:02:47.402
It is not a thing. It is a service.

00:02:47.402 --> 00:02:50.806
Amazon Dash is a service that's enabled

00:02:50.806 --> 00:02:53.156
by a dedicated device--so this is a real thing.

00:02:53.156 --> 00:02:56.156
So you can buy a washing machine from Whirlpool

00:02:56.156 --> 00:02:59.296
or GE that will reorder its own supplies.

00:02:59.296 --> 00:03:05.556
It will re-order its own Tide

00:03:05.556 --> 00:03:06.916
when it's running out of Tide.

00:03:06.916 --> 00:03:09.516
Will re-order its own bleach when it's running

00:03:09.516 --> 00:03:11.496
out of bleach. You can buy this today.

00:03:11.496 --> 00:03:14.276
This is enabled by Amazon's Dash service.

00:03:14.276 --> 00:03:16.256
And the reason that Amazon made this

00:03:16.256 --> 00:03:19.016
is so that they wouldn't have to make these devices--

00:03:19.016 --> 00:03:21.716
you know, shipping all that metal is really expensive.

00:03:21.716 --> 00:03:23.356
Why should we, making it,

00:03:23.356 --> 00:03:28.296
why should we take the hit on doing

00:03:28.296 --> 00:03:30.176
the R &amp; D for a washing machine

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.876
when we can take all the profit by selling the Tide?

00:03:32.976 --> 00:03:37.856
So Amazon also, for things that don't speak (to)

00:03:37.856 --> 00:03:41.176
the Amazon Dash service, they'll sell you a button for it.

00:03:41.176 --> 00:03:43.036
So here's a Tide button.

00:03:43.036 --> 00:03:46.256
This is a network computer you can buy

00:03:46.256 --> 00:03:49.916
for $5 whose entire purpose is to order you Tide.

00:03:49.916 --> 00:03:52.796
Every single time you push the button

00:03:52.796 --> 00:03:56.816
it will order you Tide and only Tide.

00:03:56.816 --> 00:03:59.856
Here you can pass it around.

00:03:59.856 --> 00:04:05.236
Don't be ordering me Tide!

00:04:07.756 --> 00:04:13.916
So... if you look here you can see...

00:04:13.916 --> 00:04:17.516
the top one is macaroni and cheese

00:04:17.516 --> 00:04:19.556
the bottom one is mints.

00:04:19.556 --> 00:04:24.376
These are services that are effectively preparing you

00:04:24.376 --> 00:04:26.556
for infinitely automatically

00:04:26.556 --> 00:04:29.285
replenishable macaroni and cheese.

00:04:29.285 --> 00:04:32.176
It's a macaroni and cheese service

00:04:32.176 --> 00:04:34.733
that you will buy into so you never have to think

00:04:34.733 --> 00:04:37.376
about buying macaroni and cheese again.

00:04:37.376 --> 00:04:40.276
The margins on this are insane.

00:04:40.276 --> 00:04:46.876
So most large-scale Internet of Things

00:04:46.876 --> 00:04:51.016
products are service avatars like this.

00:04:51.016 --> 00:04:53.636
They use specialized sensors and actuators

00:04:53.636 --> 00:04:57.256
to support a service. But they have very little value

00:04:57.256 --> 00:05:00.236
or don't even work at all without the supporting service.

00:05:00.236 --> 00:05:01.916
It's just like your phone.

00:05:01.916 --> 00:05:03.256
Your phone if you cancel your contract

00:05:03.256 --> 00:05:04.276
doesn't really work.

00:05:04.276 --> 00:05:05.476
I mean the Wi-Fi works, but

00:05:05.476 --> 00:05:07.336
theoretically doesn't really work.

00:05:07.336 --> 00:05:10.496
When SmartThings was acquired by Samsung,

00:05:10.496 --> 00:05:13.656
they clearly state their service offering up front.

00:05:13.656 --> 00:05:16.016
And tell you very little about what the stuff does.

00:05:16.016 --> 00:05:18.587
What the service offers is that they will help you

00:05:18.596 --> 00:05:20.096
be home wherever you are.

00:05:20.096 --> 00:05:23.316
They don't tell you how.
That's what they're going to do.

00:05:23.316 --> 00:05:24.616
What does their hardware do?

00:05:24.616 --> 00:05:26.176
You don't know. You don't care.

00:05:26.176 --> 00:05:27.576
You shouldn't care.

00:05:27.576 --> 00:05:31.616
Compare that to X10, their spiritual predecessor,

00:05:31.616 --> 00:05:34.656
who's been around since the Tandy color computer.

00:05:34.736 --> 00:05:37.756
All X10 tells you about its white plastic boxes

00:05:37.756 --> 00:05:41.076
is what they are. Not what they will accomplish for you.

00:05:41.076 --> 00:05:43.296
Like I don't even know if there is a service.

00:05:43.296 --> 00:05:45.956
Why should I care that they have "modules"?

00:05:45.956 --> 00:05:49.896
What the!? I shouldn't and I don't.

00:05:49.896 --> 00:05:54.176
So I think the real value that connected services offer

00:05:54.176 --> 00:05:57.576
is their ability to make sense of the world on our behalf.

00:05:57.576 --> 00:05:59.996
To reduce cognitive load

00:05:59.996 --> 00:06:02.456
by enabling people to interact with the world

00:06:02.456 --> 00:06:05.736
with devices at a higher level than simple data.

00:06:05.736 --> 00:06:07.256
Than simple telemetry.

00:06:07.256 --> 00:06:09.076
At the level of intentions and goals

00:06:09.076 --> 00:06:10.936
rather than data and control.

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:13.156
Humans are not built to make sense

00:06:13.156 --> 00:06:14.436
of huge amounts of data

00:06:14.436 --> 00:06:15.776
across many devices.

00:06:15.776 --> 00:06:17.976
Or to articulate our needs as systems

00:06:17.976 --> 00:06:19.976
of mutually interdependent components.

00:06:19.976 --> 00:06:20.756
Computers are great

00:06:20.756 --> 00:06:21.716
at all that shit.

00:06:30.036 --> 00:06:32.096
 

